# Uncomment the lines for the LLM provider you want to use. Pick
# exactly one approach.
#
# ⚠️  This file is tracked in git. Do NOT commit a real LOGOS_API_KEY.
#     Either keep it un-set here and `export LOGOS_API_KEY=...` in your
#     shell before `docker compose up`, or put the real value in
#     .env.local (which is gitignored).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option A: LM Studio (local, default)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run LM Studio on your machine with a model loaded. The llm container
# reaches it via host.docker.internal:1234 (compose default).
# Override LLM_MODEL only if the model id in LM Studio differs from
# gemma-4-e2b. Nothing here is required for the default setup.
#
# LLM_MODEL=gemma-4-e2b
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option B: Logos (TUM-hosted openai/gpt-oss-120b)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Setting LOGOS_API_KEY is enough — the llm service switches to
# https://logos.aet.cit.tum.de/v1/chat/completions and the
# openai/gpt-oss-120b model automatically, overriding the LM Studio
# defaults.
#
# Off-campus you must be connected to eduVPN; the Logos prod instance
# is only reachable from the TUM network.
#
# LOGOS_API_KEY=lg-...
